From dfa9325cccaff0c0bd6075e6dc79c1a15067cb7b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tarpediem <tarpediem@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 11:49:13 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 16/17] dmaengine: qcom: gpi: let the DT override the EE offset

Read the optional qcom,gpi-ee-offset property after the match data.
On the Galaxy Tab S7+ the sm8250 default of 0 makes every GPI command
time out (EV ALLOCATE completion timeout); the stock kernel uses
0x1000 for the QUPv3_0 GPI.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/dma/qcom/gpi.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/dma/qcom/gpi.c b/drivers/dma/qcom/gpi.c
index a5055a627..1202ec908 100644
--- a/drivers/dma/qcom/gpi.c
+++ b/drivers/dma/qcom/gpi.c
@@ -2190,6 +2190,13 @@ static int gpi_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	}
 
 	ee_offset = (uintptr_t)device_get_match_data(gpi_dev->dev);
+	/*
+	 * The EE offset depends on how the firmware partitions the GSI between
+	 * execution environments; some boards differ from the SoC default (and
+	 * from one QUP wrapper to the next). Let the DT override it.
+	 */
+	of_property_read_u32(gpi_dev->dev->of_node, "qcom,gpi-ee-offset",
+			     &ee_offset);
 	gpi_dev->ee_base = gpi_dev->ee_base - ee_offset;
 
 	gpi_dev->ev_factor = EV_FACTOR;
-- 
